# NG-RT-REFRACTION: ray-traced refraction of glass and shop windows, day half (designs
# F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3C-DESIGN.md, F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3B-DESIGN.md and F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION3-DESIGN.md,
# «## Приёмка»; physics F:/aftmp/NG-RT-REFRACTION2-DESIGN.md). One editor session in F:/BistroFoliageProj,
# B16_Bistro_Street: frames of the shop window - path tracer | Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced
# | HardwareTraced with Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 | HardwareTraced again | HardwareTraced with
# Reflections.HitLighting 1 | HardwareTraced and path tracer with the shop window deleted - one camera, one
# exposure, one time, one tier.
# The knockout of [day_rt] (3C D4). "day_rt differs from day_ss" is not a statement: the hit the camera sees reads
# the same scene copy, a thin sheet does not bend the ray, the tint is the same BaseColor - day_rt / day_ss 2.71
# against a run noise of 3.86. The trace is proven by switching its answer off in the same session instead:
# day_rt_mute is HardwareTraced with Translucency.RefractionComposite 0 (the glass cell ignores the trace), day_rt_b
# is day_rt again 512 frames later with the camera still (the run noise). Measure: mean |delta| of (R+G+B)/3
# (0..255) over the pane mask = rectangle x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where day_pt > 8; |day_rt - day_rt_mute| >=
# 2 x |day_rt - day_rt_b|.
# The path tracer is the reference: GlobalIllumination + Reflections PathTraced (the tracer pairs them). The raster
# frames keep Reflections / GI HardwareTraced; only Translucency.Refraction changes between day_ss and day_rt.
# The tier (D7): every group of the preset is pinned at High before any row (a group level drops that group's rows,
# so the pins come first); the benchmark preset (perf index 45 and 89 on one GPU within 8 minutes) chooses
# nothing in this run. An unattended run keeps every Quality change in this process (QualityState::KeepInSession):
# machine.json is never written; the tail still clears the rows. There is no group "Level" command: the next run
# starts from the machine's own selection.
# D1: Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0 is set on purpose (the Low / Medium value; High alone would give 1).
# HardwareTraced refraction must draw the front layer it needs by itself - the day proves the consumer declares its
# dependency, it is never pinned to 1 here.
# The window rule (D6): a GPU time is a budget number only when the window is free - in BOTH dumps of a pair (ss
# and rt) "ClearMainFramebuffer" <= 0.2 ms, and their "GPU frame" differ by less than 2x; else the number is not
# a measurement and the run is repeated. Budget at 1080p = ms x 2073600 / (viewport width x height), the
# viewport size from editor.log (1787x657 today = 1.17 Mpx). Every measured capture has its own profile-dump
# (reply line_NNN_profile-dump.txt) right before it.
# The measure of [refr_pt] (3C D5). The absolute brightness of the glass measures the lighting of the scene behind
# the window, not the refraction: without the glass the raster floor behind the window is dark where the path
# tracer's is sunlit (3C D6, open). A ratio L(glass) / L(open) mixes transmission with the additive reflection and
# divides by that dark floor: linear (sRGB-decoded) means of the frames scn-1127-204226 read PT glass 0.2240 / open
# 0.1921, raster 0.0782 / 0.0416 - ratio 1.17 against 1.88. What the glass ADDS is the same in both renderers: PT
# +0.0319, raster +0.0367 (+15 %). So the day compares the additive measure A = L_lin(glass) - L_lin(open),
# L_lin = mean of the sRGB-decoded (R+G+B)/3 (0..1) over the pane mask (x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where
# day_pt > 8): A(day_rt, day_rt_open) within ±25 % of A(day_pt, day_pt_open). The open frames delete the entity
# _4711 (Entity "Delete"); the scene is never saved. The night half stays absolute (night_rt to night_pt): there
# the raster and the path tracer agree on the scene.
# refl_hit: Reflections.HitLighting 1 (the Cinematic value) builds - the reflection method does not refuse.
# Frame wait: `frames N` (N presented frames). Every capture stands >= 256 frames after the last
# GlobalIllumination.Method switch (GI accumulation converged; else the opaque pixels drift).
# The camera faces the cafe shop window Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_bottom_4711
# (MASTER_Glass_Exterior, StaticMeshGlass; pane pivot -108,197,-719, centre ~y 320) from 3 m out on the terrace.
# One exposure: AutoExposure off (at the scene's own ManualExposureEV100), back on in the tail. The night half is
# NG-RT-REFRACTION-NIGHT.scn: a `set` dirties the scene, and Open Scene would stop at its confirm popup.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Textures High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Filtering High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shadows High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PostProcess High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Effects High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ViewDistance High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: AntiAliasing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: ResolutionScale High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Shading High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: PathTracing High"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Foliage High"
Дано run Anti-Aliasing "Anti-Aliasing: TAA"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Resolution.Percent 100"
Дано run Quality "Quality: Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0"
# The profile-dumps carry GPU times only with GPU profiling on (Profiler "GPU"; off, every scope reads gpu 0.000).
Дано run Debug "GPU profiling: On"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -370,300,-861
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.8806,0.07,0.4738
Дано set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure false
# --- day: path tracer | ScreenSpace | HardwareTraced
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method PathTraced"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид day_pt day, path tracer: the reference frame of the shop window - the interior behind the glass (tables, frames, bottles) where the glass refracts it
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид day_ss day, Translucency.Refraction ScreenSpace, front layer reflections off (Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0): the screen-space frame beside day_rt (not a knockout side: the same scene copy, 3C D4) - mean L of the glass area vs day_pt recorded; profile-dump: the window rule (ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms)
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction HardwareTraced"
Когда frames 256
Когда profile-dump
Тогда-вид day_rt day, HardwareTraced under Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer 0: the preset row does not stop it - the refracted interior behind the shop window, day_rt vs day_rt_mute on the glass at least 2x day_rt vs day_rt_b (mean |delta| over the pane mask, see the head); editor.log has no line "the glass refracts the scene copy"; profile-dump: "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" executed with a non-zero GPU time, the window rule holds against the day_ss dump (GPU frame within 2x, ClearMainFramebuffer <= 0.2 ms)
# --- the knockout of day_rt (3C D4): the trace's answer off, then day_rt again - the camera does not move
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite 0"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид day_rt_mute day, HardwareTraced, Translucency.RefractionComposite 0: the glass cell ignores the trace and shows the screen copy - the knockout side of [day_rt]
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite Level"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид day_rt_b day, HardwareTraced again, 512 frames after day_rt, the camera still: day_rt vs day_rt_b (mean |delta| over the pane mask) is the run noise [day_rt] is held to
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.9940,0.07,0.1094
Когда frames 32
Тогда-вид day_rt_edge day, HardwareTraced, camera yawed 22 degrees: the window at the frame's edge - the interior beyond the frame's edge is seen through the glass (under ScreenSpace that is a stretched edge)
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.8806,0.07,0.4738
# --- reflections with hit lighting (3B D3): the variant builds, the glass is not darker than day_rt
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.HitLighting 1"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид refl_hit day, HardwareTraced, Reflections.HitLighting 1: editor.log has no "did not build" and no "refused" line about SSR / SSRTrace; mean L of the glass area not below day_rt
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.HitLighting Level"
# --- day without the shop window: the denominators of T (the scene is not saved)
Когда run Entity "Delete Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Building_01_paris_building_01_bottom_4711"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид day_rt_open day, HardwareTraced, the shop-window entity _4711 deleted: the raster scene behind the window - the denominator of T(day_rt)
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method PathTraced"
Когда frames 256
Тогда-вид day_pt_open day, path tracer, the shop-window entity _4711 deleted: the reference scene behind the window - the denominator of T(day_pt)
Тогда refr_pt A = L_lin(glass) - L_lin(open) over the pane mask (x540-1260 y170-630, pixels where day_pt > 8; L_lin = mean of the sRGB-decoded (R+G+B)/3, 0..1): A(day_rt, day_rt_open) within ±25 % of A(day_pt, day_pt_open) (+15 % in scn-1127-204226); night_rt within ±25 % of night_pt (absolute, NG-RT-REFRACTION-NIGHT.scn of the same build); scripts/Dev/frames_compare.py
# --- tail: view mode and the rows back to the tier (the group pins live in this process only, see the head)
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.Refraction Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Translucency.RefractionComposite Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.TranslucentFrontLayer Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.HitLighting Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Reflections.Method Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method Level"
Когда run Quality "Quality: Resolution.Percent Level"
Когда run Debug "GPU profiling: Off"
Когда set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.AutoExposure true
Тогда rt_reset Quality and View mode reset; editor.log 0 VUID over the whole run; the pass "Translucency: Ray Traced Refraction" executed (no "did not execute" line naming it); no line refusing Translucency.Refraction HardwareTraced
